\DOC ACCUMULATEX_ARITH_TAC

\TYPE {ACCUMULATEX_ARITH_TAC : term list -> string -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
{ACCUMULATEX_ARITH_TAC excls s} rewrites the goal's assumptions describing
low-level word arithmetic for the state named {s}, replacing them by abstract
named summands/products plus an arithmetic equation relating them.

\DESCRIBE
{excls : term list} lists terms to be excluded from consideration (often
empty); {s : string} names the state whose assumptions are processed. The
conclusion is left untouched and only the assumption list changes: assumptions
whose right-hand sides are concrete word expressions (products split into
low/high halves, sums with carry, differences with borrow) are deleted, and in
their place are appended assumptions of the form {t = u}, where each {u} is a
fresh abstract constant named after {s}, together with one new real-arithmetic
assumption equating a power-of-two-weighted combination of the fresh constants
to the arithmetic expression they stand for; flag assumptions mentioning the
same expression are rewritten to mention the fresh carry constant. Typically
two or three assumptions are removed and two or three added at the end of the
list.
{
   A ?- t
   ========================  ACCUMULATEX_ARITH_TAC excls s
   A' ?- t
}
\noindent where {A'} is {A} with the matched assumptions replaced as described.

\FAILURE
Fails with a search failure ({tryfind}) when no assumption matches any of the
arithmetic patterns sought under the given state name and exclusion list, i.e.
the chosen state's assumptions contain no word expression of the kinds it can
abstract; this is seen for both empty and non-empty exclusion lists.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces this one-goal, assumption-rewriting behaviour is the
only behaviour, always on goals whose conclusion is an {eventually}
machine-step statement with the given state name.

\ENDDOC
